      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-252745",
      ":question/problem": "Let $X_{1}$, $X_{2}$, $X_{3}$ be three numbers chosen independently and uniformly at random from the interval $[0, 1]$. What is the probability that the third order statistic $X_{(3)}$ is less than $\\frac{1}{2}$?\n\nHint: The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[0, 1]$ is given by\n\n$f(x) = {1,\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le x \\le 1, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
